<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luis Sánchez Cerro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1889–1933</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Luis Miguel Sánchez Cerro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luis Sánchez Cerro was a Peruvian army officer who overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-b-leguia">Augusto B. Leguía</a> in August 1930 and, after a brief exile, won the disputed presidential election of 1931 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-raul-haya-de-la-torre">Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre</a>. His government harshly repressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-popular-revolutionary-alliance">APRA</a>, including after the Trujillo uprising of 1932, and went to war with Colombia over Leticia. He was assassinated by a young APRA member in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in April 1933.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luis-sanchez-cerro.jpg" alt="Luis Sánchez Cerro" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Toño Zapata (republished in 1999) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C3%A1nchez_Cerro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
